VERDICT: UNSUPPORTED -- the x230v2-28GS has no fixed copper (RJ45) switchport; copper reaches
         it only through SFP modules, and an SFP is a pluggable transceiver, not a fixed copper
         port, so MDI/MDI-X does not apply to it
      fixed copper switchport on the DUT ..... none  (switchports are SFP cages; the two links
                                                      used run through AT-SPTXa / AT-SPTXc modules)
      DUT forced polarity mdi / mdix ......... refused  (% Polarity set failed port1.0.1 / port1.0.8;
                                                      "Polarity mode not supported on this interface")
      auto at both ends, through the modules . links up  (0004 TC1, TC6 crossover; 0003 TC1, TC11
                                                      straight: framework PASS)
      partner forced mdi, DUT auto ........... link up 1000/full on the crossover lead
      speed/duplex, through the modules ...... 0003 TC6, TC7, TC8 framework PASS; TC9, TC10
                                                      (10 Mb/s) NOT RUN
      forced-polarity TestCases .............. 0004 TC2-5, 0003 TC2-5 UNSUPPORTED (each starts
                                                      with DUT `polarity mdi|mdix`)
NEEDS:   a fixed copper 10/100/1000BASE-T (RJ45) switchport on the DUT, whose MDI/MDI-X role can
         be left on auto, forced with `polarity mdi|mdix`, and read back as `current polarity`.
ABSENT:  the DUT's switchports (port1.0.1-port1.0.28) are SFP cages; copper is present only as
         pluggable transceivers, ruled by the Test Engineer not to be fixed copper ports for
         MDI/MDI-X. The populated cages, including the two this case used (1.0.1, 1.0.8):
