CAVEAT:  The framework TestCases that PASS (0004 TC1, TC6; 0003 TC1, TC6, TC7, TC8, TC11)
         exercise the copper SFP modules in the DUT's SFP cages. By the ruling above those are
         not fixed copper ports, so these PASSes do not make the case PASS; they are recorded as
         this run's measurements of the pluggable modules. The DUT reports "current polarity
         auto" on both modules throughout, so its own resolved MDI/MDI-X role was never visible;
         only the partner's was. 10 Mb/s was not exercised. The partner was forced to mdi only,
         and only on the crossover lead. The run printed the populated cages only (1.0.1-1.0.8);
         that port1.0.9-port1.0.28 are cages too is the platform fact the ruling rests on, not a
         line of this run's output.

